00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:49.440
it, that's how you know it's not real.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:51.760
So, here are 10 lessons I learned from

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.840
being married for 10 years. The simplest

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:55.600
days are the best. When you're

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.040
practicing your love for one another in

00:09:55.600 --> 00:10:00.640
your own ways, those are the best days.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:03.920
I can seriously care less if he sent me

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:06.240
a truckload of roses or buy some bags

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:08.640
for me. I really don't care about grand

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.520
gestures. And that's also how women get

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:13.000
manipulated. They think that's love.

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:14.600
There are statistics that show the more

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.840
money you spend on weddings, the more

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:19.720
likely it is to be divorced. None of it

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.880
is really necessary and often times can

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.760
be covering up for real issues that only

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.000
come up when you strip everything else

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.320
down. Pete and I were so simple

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:30.240
together, so easy. We got married in

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.960
city hall, nothing fancy at all. I

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.160
thrifted the dress that I wore that day

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.920
and nobody can take our marriage from us

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.840
because it's not attached to the

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:40.200
material world. You notice how sometimes

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:44.440
people's relationships fall apart when

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:46.040
one of them loses a job or becomes broke

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.680
or something like that. Yeah, that's not

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:50.360
us. Not money, not our looks or even our

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.400
backgrounds or the things that we have.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:54.520
We didn't marry each other for that. He

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:56.680
married me at, in my opinion, my

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.440
physical worst, okay? And neither of us

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.800
had much money at the time. So, it

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.280
wasn't like we could have a lavish

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.280
wedding or anything, but we also didn't

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:04.680
need it. All we have is we love one

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:06.240
another, we don't give up on each other,

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:08.240
we help each other get better, and isn't

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.360
that the best thing ever? Who cares

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.440
about anything else when you can have

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.120
the best? When you're making coffee for

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.720
another without even being asked, when

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.880
we keep each other comfortable in all

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:19.160
the ways, out of love and respect for

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.360
one another, consideration and regard,

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:23.200
and sitting together, watching TV in

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.720
just comfortable silence. Because when

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.280
you're having a nice time, you don't

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:28.160
have to say anything to try and make up

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.920
for the silence and be performative

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.800
because what's there to perform? So,

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.520
these simple days are the ones you

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:35.640
should be keeping score of, not the

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:37.880
fights, not the did you buy me a rose

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:39.520
this week, because that's not what our

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.520
relationship is built on. I remember one

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:43.360
time, we were in Venice and he bought me

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:44.800
roses and I don't know why I got so mad

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.360
at him because I was like, you really

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.280
didn't have to do that and it means

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.920
nothing to me. In hindsight, maybe I

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:51.720
shouldn't have gotten so mad. I was kind

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.600
of mean, honestly, but at the time I

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.720
still had my anger issues and it was

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:57.320
also very sweet of him to do that, but I

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:59.080
just didn't want our relationship to

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:01.120
start going in that way of like, what

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.920
can you do for me and what can I do for

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.760
you in return? It's very transactional

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.440
and constant transaction is the very

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.760
last thing that I want when it comes to

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:09.360
our relationship, when it comes to

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:11.160
marriage. You have to spend your life

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.800
with this person. That's what you agreed

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:14.280
to and if there's something about the

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:15.680
marriage that can't be reconciled, like

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:17.640
you have to ask yourself, like what's

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:19.200
worth it to you? I love the consistency

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.680
and the mundane devotion. That's the

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.400
most beautiful part of a marriage. You

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:24.000
also marry multiple versions of the same

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.520
person and that person will be different

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.720
again in three to five years, by the

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:29.520
way. Change is the only constant. If you

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.960
expect someone's personality to never

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.760
change, you will suffer because they

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:35.280
won't end up like what you expect them

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:37.200
to be, unless they are a fixed sign in

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:38.400
astrology, then maybe they will, but

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.920
seriously though, if you expect your

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.040
relationship to evolve and grow, then

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:44.360
you need to hold space for your partner

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:45.960
to grow, too. That way you will also

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.360
both evolve together and grow together

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:48.720
instead of growing apart. I think that's

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:50.160
really important because not only do we

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:52.040
have to work on ourselves, our

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.839
identities, but it's also you and them.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.440
That's an identity that you both share

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:58.240
together and there are certain aspects

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:59.960
of my old self that I had to let go of.

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:01.520
I spent years building this identity of

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.480
like a hyper-independent woman who

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:04.960
doesn't need anybody, who has anger

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.040
issues or whatever. I could just handle

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:09.360
everything myself, you know, even though

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:10.920
realistically, I could use some help

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.520
here and there, but I wanted to stay in

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:15.720
control and my marriage stripped all of

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:17.600
that away because me feeling safe enough

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:19.560
in the relationship made it impossible

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:21.640
to keep putting up walls like that. I

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.480
had to confront myself that this

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:25.720
independence of mine was a trauma

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:27.680
response and coming out of my own

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.400
hyper-vigilance. I didn't want to be

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.160
vulnerable enough for someone to

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:33.960
actually hurt me, but I had to feel safe

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.840
enough to know that he wouldn't hurt me.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.080
And even if he did, so what? We can talk

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.480
about it. Because if you don't feel

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.160
comfortable enough to talk things

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.240
through with your partner and talk about

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.640
anything, then that's kind of a red flag

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.800
in my opinion. But at least you know

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.400
that you don't have to pull up walls

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.920
anymore. You can build something

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:51.040
together with someone and be a team.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:53.520
Love is also a practice. It's not just

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:56.480
an emotion and not just affection, but

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:59.040
also the constant practice of patience,

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.680
regulation, showing up as your best self

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:03.240
for your better half, teamwork,

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:05.120
logistics, being able to handle all

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.160
kinds of projects and things that happen

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.680
in our lives including the good and the

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.720
bad and showing up for something greater

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:12.920
than yourself. And that greater purpose

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:15.360
is us. It's the marriage. Because the

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:17.160
feelings of, you know, crushes and

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:19.040
infatuation, none of these things matter

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.880
in the long run. It just comes and goes.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.760
But true love is a practice that carries

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:26.040
you through all of the weeks that you

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:27.640
feel terrible and the other person will

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.520
understand that and can hold space for

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:31.200
it or better yet help you through it.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:33.240
Good communication is also not saying

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.480
whatever comes to your mind. So one big

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.640
thing about our marriage is that he

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:37.720
taught me how to communicate better.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.720
Because remember when I said I had

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:41.640
really bad anger issues? I said it like

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.440
a million times, but I would say the

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:47.800
nastiest things in fights and act out a

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:49.120
lot because I didn't know how to show up

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:51.040
properly. Like I didn't grow up in a

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.600
stable household and wasn't shown good

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:55.440
examples of how to behave in

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.640
relationships. Unfortunately, I had to

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.320
learn all of these things and I'm glad

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.280
that I learned it from the right person

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:03.040
who taught me, even though he himself

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:04.520
also didn't grow up with amazing family

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.920
either, but he had always known deep

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:07.720
down that he that's not the way things

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:10.040
should be. And you know, he deserved

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.800
better. I deserved better, too. Most

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:12.760
people think that having good

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:14.200
communication means just being super

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.160
brutally honest and just say whatever

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:18.760
you feel and hash it out, but that is

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:20.920
not good communication. But it is a form

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:22.360
of emotional dumping ground, partner is

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.680
not dumping ground. You really got to

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.440
treat each other like you're better

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:27.440
halves, and if you don't, then you got

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.320
to question like why are you together?

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.760
Like would I talk to my significant

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:33.280
other like that so rudely? So, good

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:35.320
communication in a relationship is

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:37.880
getting the message across in a way that

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:40.280
the other person can understand you and

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:42.320
hears you. So, learning to say the right

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:44.040
things that can still help you solve

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.240
whatever issues you're going through.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.960
There's actually something Pete said to

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:49.400
me recently that really made me think a

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:51.520
lot, actually. He said, "Whenever I say

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:52.880
something that's kind of mean, or I do

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:55.120
something that he doesn't really like,

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:56.200
and if it's not a big deal, like if it

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.360
doesn't get in the way of our

00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:00.520
relationship, he rehearses the

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:02.400
conversation in his head. If it doesn't

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.880
go according to what he thinks it will

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:06.960
go, he will drop it." And I asked him,

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:08.920
"Baby, why don't you just tell me, and

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:10.160
we can resolve we can talk about this."

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:12.320
And he said that he assessed the

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:15.000
situation, if it's going to somehow lead

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:17.480
into us having a bad day, into a big

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:19.720
fight, then is that tiny little remark

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:22.080
that I said really worth bringing up? He

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:23.880
can always bring it up later when I'm in

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.480
a better state of mind. And that's a

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:29.360
very, very mature of him to say that.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:31.360
Timing the conversation correctly, and

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:33.480
understanding that the delivery matters

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:35.120
as much as what you're saying. You can

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:37.000
be right about everything, logistically

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.960
speaking, and completely destroy the

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.880
conversation and ruin your day by how

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:44.280
you're saying it. Conflict is also

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.000
inevitable, but contempt is the poison.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:47.400
In relationships, you're going to fight

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:50.360
at some point, and that is not the

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:52.920
problem. How you fight matters the most.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:55.880
If you have contempt, or you build up a

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:57.160
quiet state of like hating your partner,

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:59.440
and you start looking at your partner

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:01.440
with disgust instead of with love and

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:04.560
compassion, then that is one of the

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:06.240
biggest silent killers of marriages. I

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.800
heard someone tell me this years ago

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:10.439
that every time you feel a fight coming

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:12.920
on, ask yourself one question. What's

00:17:10.439 --> 00:17:14.920
more worth it to you right now? Winning

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:17.720
or peace? Because even when you fight

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:19.560
and you win, you don't actually win.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.400
Nobody wins when you fight. You might

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:24.040
get the last word, you might prove your

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:25.959
point, but ultimately, everybody still

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.360
loses because you've created more

00:17:25.959 --> 00:17:29.200
distance. Now there's even more

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:31.200
resentment, and someone's going to bed

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.600
angry that night, and nobody wins. But

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.440
if you learn how to communicate

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:37.760
properly, then everybody wins, and isn't

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:40.840
that the best? So be gentle on the

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:42.040
communication and tough on the problem.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:43.280
These are two completely different

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:46.840
things, and it gets confused all the

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:48.480
time because instead, most people go

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:51.760
the issue. You have to flip that. We

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:53.480
have to learn to set our ego aside and

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:56.040
not try to win all the time because it's

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:57.880
not you versus me, it's us versus the

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.520
problem. The moment you start fighting

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:01.240
to win an argument instead of fighting

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:03.640
to understand each other, you've already

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:05.960
lost before the fight even starts.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:07.720
Everyone has flaws, and they have

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:10.080
limits. Every single person you will

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.880
ever be with will have something that

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:13.280
annoys you, or triggers you, or tests

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:15.720
your patience. But if it's not

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:18.280
egregiously bad, like if it's not abuse,

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:19.720
or harmful to you, or to other people in

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.400
a way that you're not qualified to help

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:24.000
with, or if it's extremely serious, then

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:25.760
we can help each other get better.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.880
That's the whole point of partnership.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:28.480
You're not looking for someone who's

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.160
perfect. Nobody's perfect. You're

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:32.200
looking for someone whose flaws you can

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:34.000
work with, and who's willing to work

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:36.120
with your flaws, too, so you can help

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.520
each other evolve. Attraction matures

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:41.360
eventually. It is not a loss. You will

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:43.480
go from novelty to feeling safe. You

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:45.160
start to develop deeper trust in each

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:47.520
other. And a lot of people do panic when

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:49.040
this happens because the spark is dying,

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:50.760
the relationship's going to get boring,

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.640
like the seven-year itch, for example.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:56.160
But you didn't lose attraction for your

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:58.400
partner, it simply matured into a more

00:18:56.160 --> 00:19:00.040
later stage, a stable stage. And a

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:02.520
stable marriage comes from staying

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:04.520
stable. A lot of us may have gotten used

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:07.080
to a lot of drama happening when we were

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:09.520
growing up, and a lot of intensity and

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.920
tea and fights. And intensity belongs to

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:13.120
a temporary infatuation. Intensity is

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:15.280
also very up and down, and very

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:16.840
stressful, and that kind of stress does

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.280
not belong in a long-term relationship

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:20.160
because you would just burn each other

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:22.800
out eventually. The deepest love that I

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.480
felt is not nervousness or butterflies

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.120
in my stomach, but just knowing deep in

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:27.800
my bones that this person is not going

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:29.720
anywhere. They're here for me. They will

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:31.280
follow me to the ends of the earth, and

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:33.200
me as well. I will do the same, and that

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:35.840
is more attractive than any rush of

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:38.480
novelty. Knowing and seeing the level of

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:40.240
devotion and how much they care about me

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:42.040
and how much I care about them. Like

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:43.720
we're not going anywhere from that. Your

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:45.920
partner also cannot be everything for

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:47.600
you. You cannot have the expectation

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:49.360
that they will do everything for you.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:51.520
That kind of expectation will kill your

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:53.840
romance. They are not your therapist.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:55.160
They are not a replacement for a butler.

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.640
They're not your only source of

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:58.320
entertainment. They can't be your only

00:19:56.640 --> 00:20:00.880
source of happiness. Or even worse, your

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:02.960
partner should not be your parent. No,

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:05.800
they're here to play the role of your

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:07.320
partner. So, if you have the desire to

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.360
go out there and live a full life and

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:11.080
live your best life to have your

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:13.040
friendships, your passions, and your own

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:14.600
growth separate from a marriage, that's

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.240
fine. But all of these things should not

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:18.600
be threatening the marriage or the

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:20.360
relationship. Instead, it should protect

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:22.680
it in the process. It takes courage to

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.720
stay, but also takes courage to leave.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:26.280
And I say this with so much care and

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:28.080
love because some of you need permission

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.720
to stay in your marriage and fight for

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.480
it. And some of you also need permission

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:33.960
to walk away from a bad relationship.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:35.560
The correct choice depends on one thing.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.760
No matter what you're going through, no

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:39.720
matter what kind of challenges you're

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:42.800
facing, are you moving towards your

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:45.120
integrity and values or straying away

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:47.040
from it? Staying out of fear is not

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:49.680
courageous, and leaving out of avoidance

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:51.320
is also not brave. But staying because

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:53.120
you believe in what you're building and

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:54.760
you recognize how good this relationship

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.960
is, how fulfilling it is for you

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:58.720
relative to anything else that you've

00:20:55.960 --> 00:21:00.240
experienced, how happy it makes you, or

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:01.880
you leave because you know that you're

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.560
not getting what you want, that you

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:05.360
should be getting something better, and

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.960
you deserve better because the other

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.680
partner is not giving back to you, and

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.440
you're not happy and they don't care

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:12.440
enough to try hard for you. Both of

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:14.880
these things are very different and they

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:16.520
both require the same level of bravery.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:19.840
There have been many times in the past

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:22.000
when we fight and I think about divorce,

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:25.000
I talk about divorce, but what kept me

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.880
staying is will I become a better person

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:29.080
without this marriage or will me leaving

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:31.080
this marriage leave me worse off in the

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:33.200
process. I am not saying that I am

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:35.560
doomed without him, but in a way it's

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:38.360
like if I'm letting go of something so

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:40.480
beautiful, am I betraying myself, too?

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.680
You really have to do that risk analysis

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.000
for yourself because everybody's

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:46.040
relationship is different, but Pete has

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.720
never given me a real reason to leave

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:49.920
and neither have I with him. A

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:51.960
long-lasting marriage is also a constant

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.680
delight. A lot of people fear staying

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:55.960
stagnant and stuck in a long-term

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:57.520
marriage because we picture it as two

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.160
people sitting on a couch watching the

00:21:57.520 --> 00:22:00.720
same show for 40 years with nothing to

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.120
say and it's boring and they want

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.320
something more exciting than that. But a

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:06.600
long-lasting relationship does not have

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:08.480
to stagnate at all. Not if you're both

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:10.680
committed to being interesting and

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:12.000
growing and surprising one another and

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:13.960
always bringing something new to the

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:16.200
table and you're keeping your curiosity

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:18.760
alive. It should all be a constant

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:20.880
delight and just having a good time and

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:22.720
not a feeling of dread where every day

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:24.240
you wish you had something different and

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:25.640
I know a lot of people go through that.

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:27.200
I think my marriage is exciting. We can

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:28.720
do everything together, we're into the

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:31.320
same things, we have the same taste in

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:32.520
music and home decor, we love to travel.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:34.120
Like if he doesn't like something I'm

